{"availability":"available","full":"pountzas/portfolio-next-react","name":"portfolio-next-react","description":"This is my new Portfolio created with NEXT.js. Used GraphQL to scrap the 6 pinned repos from my GitHub Profile.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":6,"forks":0,"created":"2022-01-25T20:09:53Z","updated":"2026-10-05T10:12:02Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pountzas-portfolio.vercel.app/","topics":["framer-motion","graphql","nextjs","reactjs","tailwind-css","vercel"],"demo":"https://pountzas-portfolio.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:27:16.910Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T21:27:16.910Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T21:27:16.910Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T21:27:16.910Z","stars":6,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project uses GraphQL to load GitHub repos onto the Projects page: the latest pinned items plus category tabs (web, mobile, desktop, dependencies). Cards render first, then fill in commit counts, GitHub release/download totals when a repo has releases, and last-year npm downloads for published packages. Click a project card and it animates out into a centered modal (and back on close) with the full description, topics, stats, and live-demo links. GitHub links are shown only for public repositories.","The Skills page groups technologies by what they ship — Languages, Web, Native Apps, Backend & Data, Tooling & Platforms, and Design — including Rust, Tauri, Firebase, and Supabase.","When I change a pinned project on GitHub, the portfolio updates on the next rebuild."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pountzas/portfolio-next-react/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5ba5af292e09a18bee12c460addac1f40005d5c0823f64a770a0bc0c97663acd","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T21:27:16.987Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:27:16.987Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project uses GraphQL t